.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-analytics-timeseries - Order counts bucketed by day, week or month


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 analytics timeseries [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Order counts over time, one row per bucket.

.PP
Each row carries a volume only when a SINGLE token and chain are filtered: summing
different tokens' base units would be meaningless, so the gateway returns null
instead of a number that looks addable.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--chain-id\fP=0
	Filter by EVM chain ID

.PP
\fB--from\fP=""
	Only payments created at/after this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for timeseries

.PP
\fB--interval\fP=""
	Bucket width: day (default), week or month

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	Filter by mode: authorize or charge

.PP
\fB--status\fP=""
	Filter by payment status (e.g. captured)

.PP
\fB--to\fP=""
	Only payments created at/before this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB--token\fP=""
	Filter by token address (0x…)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 analytics timeseries
  rail0 analytics timeseries --interval month --chain-id 5042002 --token 0x3600…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-analytics(1)\fP
